<!--
  Puts WTL on the include path for every project built from this tree, including
  the SDK's own, without editing anything under sdk/ — which matters because
  sdk/ is fetched rather than committed and gets deleted to re-fetch.

  MSBuild imports this automatically: it walks up from each .vcxproj looking for
  the nearest Directory.Build.targets, and every SDK project sits under this
  directory. `.targets` rather than `.props` on purpose: props are imported
  before Microsoft.Cpp.props and would be overwritten by it, while targets are
  imported last and win.

  This replaced setting INCLUDE with /p:UseEnv=true, which appears to work and
  then breaks the *resource* compiler: UseEnv swaps MSBuild's computed search
  paths for the environment wholesale, so rc.exe loses the Windows SDK's `um`
  directory and every .rc fails with "cannot open include file 'winres.h'" — a
  header sitting right there in the SDK, which makes it a genuinely confusing
  error to land on. Appending to $(IncludePath) leaves everything else exactly
  as the toolchain computed it.

  Note for anyone editing this comment: an XML comment may not contain two
  consecutive hyphens. Prose punctuation costs a build here.
-->
<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IncludePath>$(IncludePath);$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)sdk\wtl\Include</IncludePath>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
